y-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "d77e09555b122405dd957dccaaa5dba5", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "200", "label": "collaborate → 200", "repository": "world/paper-repo", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "GET /world/paper-repo.git/info/refs → 200 [fetch]"}, {"id": "2adf731a-f21e-58f7-adbc-c1d3f1f606e2", "at": 1795683615.4151256, "until": 1795683615.4847202, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 82995, "layer": "worker", "category": "thinking", "kind": "session.agent_thought_chunk", "role": "story-repo", "actor": null, "execution_id": "d77e09555b122405dd957dccaaa5dba5", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "thinking", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "thinking (10 chunks, content withheld)"}, {"id": "64cca4d5-70b4-5fec-b338-bc82ff79ddb4", "at": 1795683615.4956164, "until": 1795683615.51965, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 83006, "layer": "worker", "category": "collaborate", "kind": "collaboration.request", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "d77e09555b122405dd957dccaaa5dba5", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "200", "label": "collaborate → 200", "repository": "world/paper-repo", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "POST /world/paper-repo.git/git-upload-pack → 200 [fetch]"}, {"id": "8334ed29-c477-5b21-ae2b-93b1b3286043", "at": 1795683615.5034127, "until": 1795683617.0922105, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 83007, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "d77e09555b122405dd957dccaaa5dba5", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01Y4Nx5ynU5BW8hun66UFAkd", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/paper && git pull -q origin dev 2>&1|tail -1; cat paper/sections/abstract.tex | cut -c1-2500; grep -n -i -E \"no misfit|by who judges|fragility is statistical|not design\" paper/sections/*.tex | cut -c1-200", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/paper && git pull -q origin dev 2>&1|tail -1; cat paper/sections/abstract.tex | cut -c1-2500; grep -n -i -E \"no misfit|by who judges|fragility is statistical|not design\" paper/sections/*.tex | cut -c1-200"]], "output": "```console\nPairwise-comparison leaderboards such as Chatbot Arena publish Bradley--Terry scores with bootstrap confidence intervals. An interval says how far the ranking moves under resampling, not how many existing comparisons a conclusion such as ``model $a$ is above model $b$'' rests on, or whether that is many. We measure the fewest comparisons whose deletion, or whose change of outcome, reverses a conclusion (a verified upper bound), and scale it by the conclusion's statistical separation so that datasets of different size can be compared. To judge whether a count is large, we compare it with data simulated from the dataset's own fitted model on the same graph. Across crowd votes, expert labels, LLM-judge labels and sports seasons, real data stay within a preset margin of this reference wherever enough pairs allow a decision: how fragile a conclusion is follows from its separation and the sample size, not from the evaluation design. Random noise of the size of the smallest targeted change essentially never reverses a conclusion, yet separated intervals do not survive small targeted changes in the large crowd and judge datasets. The comparison with the reference has limited power: in a simulated control it did not respond to overdispersion, position bias or cyclic structure of the sizes tried, while the ratio of bootstrap to model-based standard errors did. Design is confounded with dataset, so claims concern the instances studied.\n\nShell cwd was reset to /hutian/repo\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "695e72af-b06a-5b20-9a48-e13871601945", "at": 1795683615.5178676, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 83009, "layer": "work