41637bc1-1965-576a-b1c9-bb5864cb936a", "at": 1795683621.481298, "until": 1795683625.7686043, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 83046, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "d77e09555b122405dd957dccaaa5dba5", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01XJmwzubjhjToPdv15iJXF4", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/story-wiki && forge issue create -R world/paper-repo -t \"Abstract: 'not from the evaluation design' is the headline Outline rev 17 withdrew\" -b \"Outline rev 17 (review 5, \\`story-repo\\`#9). In the abstract of dev 9376bc1: 'how f…", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/story-wiki && forge issue create -R world/paper-repo -t \"Abstract: 'not from the evaluation design' is the headline Outline rev 17 withdrew\" -b \"Outline rev 17 (review 5, \\`story-repo\\`#9). In the abstract of dev 9376bc1: 'how fragile a conclusion is follows from its separation and the sample size, not from the evaluation design'. The positive control shows Δ is also ≈ 0 under injected design-like misfit, and Q is pinned near 1 by the first-order identity, so this sentence is not something the data can show; the limit sits two sentences later, not in it. Suggested wording: 'the count of comparisons per unit of separation follows the same-graph reference within the margin, as a first-order identity makes largely expected; the evaluation design acts on how wide the interval is (bootstrap SE over model SE: MT-Bench human 1.30 against 1.0 to 1.05 for crowd, LLM and sports... use the figures from se_ratio.csv), not on that count'. Please check the same claim in the intro findings and discussion ('is what the model of the dataset's own graph predicts' is fine; any 'not by design' phrase is not). Counts, numbers and the ±0.15 margin are unchanged.\" 2>&1|tail -1"]], "output": "